heart-tts (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release. "Read Aloud" text-to-speech for the Raspberry Pi, packaged
    from the native audio.cpp sanoTTS engine:
    - read-aloud: a floating Wayland window; highlight text anywhere, click READ.
    - heart-say: speak text (or the clipboard) aloud from the terminal.
    - heart-tts-doctor: health check + synthesis self-test.
  * Bundles the "heart" and "heart-nano" voice models (GPL-3, ampixa/sanoTTS).
    The audio.cpp engine is Apache-2.0 (ShugoAI LLC).
  * Playback through PipeWire (pw-play) so it follows the current output device
    and mixes with other audio, with an ALSA fallback.

